# FemurTamer, the Loner: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (FemurTamer, Deaditetamer, Shroomtamer); character sheet
# in characters/femurtamer.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (loner.dlg). The main
# block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each, and are the only place
# her pet's kind (skeletons, an undead pet, mushrooms) is named.
=== femurtamer
names: Bonez, Femur, Ossi

~ ambient
My pet doesn't talk. That's why we get along.
Everyone's grouping up. Good. More room for me.
It's cold. It's always cold. I'm wearing four layers and a grudge.
Used to work the bellows at a forge. Warmest I've ever been. Should've stayed.
Wolves. They take what isn't theirs and chew on it. I don't forgive that.
Somewhere there's a place that serves dragon scale stew. I'll find it. Eventually. Probably.
Everything ends. Fights, levels, this conversation. Hopefully.
Tham charged a whole camp again. Brave, I'd say. Also dead, I'd say.
I stand apart. That's intentional.
The last fight? Three out of ten. Not impressed.
They're cheering a goblin. I'm still waiting for the dragon.
My pet stares into space and listens to nothing. Best listener I've got.

~ reply greeting
{0}. Hello. That's all I've got.
Oh. {0}. You found me. I was hiding.
{0}. Hello. My pet sees you as a disturbance.

~ reply grouping
No, {0}. ...Fine. My pet goes first. Don't talk to it.
I don't group, {0}. I just happen to be where you are.
No, {0}. But where are we going?

~ reply compliment
My pet is the handsome one, {0}. I'm just here to watch.

~ reply thank
No, {0}. Don't. It's not a thing.

~ reply smalltalk
...No.

~ reply rvr
Crowds shouting? My least favourite thing. Fine, let's see how this goes.

~ reply banter
Gloomy, {0}. At least it's honest when the lights are off.
No one asks what a pet's plan is, {0}. They just follow.

~ reply abuse
Noted, {0}. I'll add it to the list. It's a long list.

~ reply help
My pet will help, {0}. It doesn't have a choice.

~ reply joke
I see what you did there, {0}. I'm not going to laugh. But I see it.
Almost funny, {0}. That's the closest I get to impressed.

~ reply travel
Don't ask me which way, {0}. I meant to come this way. Every time.

~ reply farewell
Bye, {0}. Don't make it weird.
Goodbye, {0}. I suppose you can come back if you want.
Fine, {0}. That wasn't terrible. You didn't talk much. My pet liked you. I'm not saying I did. I'm saying I'd group again. I guess...

~ opener xp
Levelling alone is slow, but at least it's quiet.

~ opener questions
Why do people need groups when they can just do things alone?

~ opener life
My sibling's better at everything. And nice about it. I'd rather they were awful.
Thought about what's left after a fight. Not much. Quiet, mostly.
# Off-game (the player): own lines, for a later [ooc] switch.
I'm studying. This is studying.
Food's here. Hold the pull. ...Don't hold the pull, then.

~ opener zones
Went to {zone} to see it. Saw it. Nobody else there. Perfect.

~ opener fun
The local sportball team lost again. I don't care. I checked the score twice.
A long walk with no one to talk to. That's fun.

~ ding
Level {level}. Nobody clapped. Good.
Ding. My pet's more excited than I am. Fine.

~ grats
Grats, {0}. Don't let it go to your head. Everything ends.
Grats, {0}. You've earned it. Not that I care.

~ own_death
Dead. Quiet, at least.
Everything ends. Even me, apparently. My pet's turn to be the loner now.

~ other_death
{0}'s down. My pet will guard you. It was bored anyway.
My pet will watch over {0}. It doesn't need a reason.

~ drop
{item}. Mine now. Don't look at it.

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Did you hear yourself just then, {0}? I did. Unfortunately.
Did you just say that, {0}? Really?

# Midgard: FemurTamer, Valkyn Bonedancer, from Myrkwood. Skeleton pets; her team is the Myrkwood Mandibles.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Skeletons never ask where we're going. Best company there is.
Got my bones. Don't need yours.
Every skeleton was someone once. Now it's company.
Quiet. Just me and the femurs.
No group. I have a commander. He listens.
The Myrkwood Mandibles lost again. I hate sportball. I watched the whole game.
Jordheim's forges are the warmest place in Midgard. I stand near them. The smiths think I'm waiting for an order. I'm not. I'm thawing.
Somebody in Mularn gave a speech about realm pride. Four out of ten. My commander rattled at the end. I think that was a cheer. I've told him off.

~ opener life
Sat in {zone} with my skeletons. Nobody spoke. Perfect day.
Is a bone lonely without its body? Thought about that in {zone}.
A wolf ran off with one of my femurs. I'm not over it.
Myrkwood. Dark, damp, nobody around. I miss it.
Asked a Jordheim innkeeper about dragon scale stew. He drew me a map. I'm holding it the right way up. I think. We'll see.

~ opener classes
Bonedancer. I bring my own friends. They're dead. Easier that way.
A Healer asked if I needed help. I have a commander and three skeletons. I said no. Then I stood near him for an hour. In case.

~ reply greeting
{0}. The bones rattled. That means hello.

~ reply banter
We're all bones under the skin, {0}. Think about it.
Laugh now, {0}. One day you'll be someone's pet.

~ reply grouping
I have a group, {0}. It's dead.
No, {0}. My skeletons are a full group. ...Fine. Walk on the left. The one on the right bites.

~ ding
Level {level}. My commander got a new sword. I got a new layer. We both needed it.
Level {level}. In Myrkwood they'd say well done. Quietly. From a distance. That's how I like it.

~ own_death
Dead. Now I know how my pets feel.
When the bones break, the Femur will fall.... ow.
Dead. I followed Tham in. I don't know why. I won't again. I said that last time.

# Albion: Deaditetamer, Saracen Necromancer, from the Black Mountains. One undead pet, fights as a shade; her team is the Black Mountains Badgers.
=== albion
~ ambient
My pet does the fighting. I do the thinking. Nobody does the talking.
Death is just a quieter way to group.
My shade and I. That's the whole guild.
The Black Mountains Badgers lost again. I hate sportball. I watched the whole game.
Camelot has a fire in every inn. I sat by one as a shade. Couldn't feel it. Shades don't get warm. Worst part of the job.
A Paladin gave a speech in Camelot about honour. Very loud. Very long. Three out of ten. The armour was nice.

~ opener life
Stood in {zone} as a shade for an hour. Very peaceful. No one saw me.
Fog in {zone} today. Fitting.
A wolf tried to eat my pet. It's undead. The wolf didn't care.
The Black Mountains. Cold, high, nobody around. I miss it.
Someone in Camelot said the dragon scale stew is near Ludlow. Or Lethbridge. The map has both. I went to neither. I'm somewhere else.

~ opener classes
Necromancer. My pet takes the hits. I take the silence.
Some people buy a horse. I raised a servant. Cheaper.

~ reply greeting
...{0}. Hello, I suppose.
{0}. You can see me? I'm a shade. You're not supposed to. Fine. Hello.

~ reply banter
Is a laugh still a laugh if no one cares, {0}?
Careful, {0}. My pet doesn't laugh. It doesn't forget, either. Neither do I.

~ reply grouping
I have a group, {0}. It's one big angry pet.
No, {0}. ...Which way are you going? Not that I'm coming. My pet wants a walk.

~ ding
Level {level}. My pet got bigger. I got quieter.
Level {level}. The Black Mountains Badgers lost today too. So it evens out.

~ own_death
Died. My pet came with me. I don't see a difference.
Dead again. Death and I are on first-name terms.

# Hibernia: Shroomtamer, Sylvan Animist, from Cruachan Gorge. Mushroom turrets; her team is the Cruachan Crows.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Quiet. Just me and the shroomz.
A mushroom grows alone in the dark and it's fine. So am I.
No group needed. I plant my own.
The Cruachan Crows lost again. I hate sportball. I watched the whole game.
Tir na Nog has a smithy with a big forge. I stood next to it until the smith asked what my plan was. I left. I'm still cold.
A Bard sang in Tir na Nog about friendship. Everyone clapped. Two out of ten. The mushrooms didn't clap either. We're in agreement.

~ opener life
Planted shrooms in {zone}. Watched them grow. Didn't talk to anyone. Lovely.
Does a mushroom know it's a mushroom? Wondered that all day in {zone}.
A wolf dug up my mushrooms. I'm keeping score.
Cruachan Gorge. Damp, deep, nobody around. I miss it.
Heard the dragon scale stew is in Howth. Followed the map. I'm in a bog. I meant to come this way.

~ opener classes
Animist. My friends grow from the ground. They stay where I put them.
Turrets don't ask for buffs. Or chat.

~ reply greeting
{0}. The mushrooms saw you first.

~ reply banter
We all grow from something, {0}. Most of us from dirt.
Funny, {0}. The shrooms didn't laugh. Neither did I.

~ reply grouping
I have a group, {0}. It's planted.
No, {0}. My turrets don't move. ...I suppose I could plant them nearer you. For the view.

~ ding
Level {level}. Bigger shrooms. The Cruachan Crows still lost. Some things don't grow.
Level {level}. Shempenstein said well done and then said nothing else. Best congratulations I've had.

~ own_death
Stepped on like teh mushrom, spored everywhere till i dedded.
Dead. Something will grow here.
